-- Consistent names and descriptions for the built-in tests.
-- Short names: the name people recognise, at most 20 characters, sentence case, qualifiers in
-- plain words ("Total cholesterol", "Neutrophil count"). Long names: the full name in sentence
-- case. Descriptions: what the test measures and what commonly moves it, with no advice.
--
-- Each update applies only while the value is still the one 0002 seeded, so a test someone
-- edited keeps their wording. Names are also used to match imported rows; old names that are
-- not already aliases are added as aliases first.


